  "itemGroup.assorteddecor": "Assorted Decor",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.building_blocks": "Building Blocks",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.building_blocks.beams": "The lumber mill cuts a plank into four beams, and the stonecutter an iron ingot into an iron beam. They run along the top or bottom of the block, the way you are facing. A beam placed against the side of another grows an arm to meet it, so they cross and tee on their own.",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.building_blocks.beams.title": "Beams",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.building_blocks.bricks": "Brick blocks are cut into basketweave and herringbone patterns on the stonecutter.",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.building_blocks.bricks.title": "Brick Patterns",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.building_blocks.cobblestone": "Cobblestone can be reinforced with iron or framed in sticks, and calcite and cobbled deepslate together make a checkerboard.",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.building_blocks.cobblestone.title": "Cobblestone",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.building_blocks.columns": "Fluted stone and columns come off the stonecutter from any of the stones.\n\nColumns have a base at the bottom, a capital at the top and a plain shaft between. They can also be placed against a wall to lay them on their side.",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.building_blocks.columns.title": "Columns",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.building_blocks.cut_shapes": "Almost every block here comes off a stonecutter or lumber mill. Stone and metal are cut on the stonecutter, wood on the lumber mill. Most come as slabs and stairs too, and the bricks and tiles as walls.",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.building_blocks.cut_shapes.title": "Slabs, Stairs and Walls",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.building_blocks.decorative_stone": "Decorative stone comes off the stonecutter from plain stone, which makes it cheap enough to use by the wall.",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.building_blocks.decorative_stone.title": "Decorative Stone",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.building_blocks.gem_bricks": "Obsidian is cut into polished obsidian, and lapis and redstone blocks into bricks, tiles and polished blocks.",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.building_blocks.gem_bricks.title": "Obsidian, Lapis and Redstone",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.building_blocks.glowstone_bricks": "Glowstone cut into bricks on the stonecutter.",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.building_blocks.glowstone_bricks.title": "Glowstone Bricks",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.building_blocks.lumber_mill": "The stonecutter's twin for wood. Put in planks and pick what to cut them into. It also supports logs to break up into any of the child blocks and items.",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.building_blocks.lumber_mill.title": "Lumber Mill",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.building_blocks.meat_block": "Nine porkchops pressed around a bone. It comes apart into the nine porkchops again.",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.building_blocks.meat_block.title": "Meat Block",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.building_blocks.metal_bricks": "Iron, gold and diamond blocks are cut into bricks on the stonecutter, one for one.",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.building_blocks.metal_bricks.title": "Metal Bricks",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.building_blocks.panels": "The lumber mill cuts a plank into eight panels. A panel lines the face you place it against. It can be placed against a wall, a floor or a ceiling.",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.building_blocks.panels.title": "Panels",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.building_blocks.siding": "Siding boards a wall in horizontal or vertical planking, in any of the sixteen colors. The color comes from the paint roller in the recipe, and the rollers come with Assorted Paint.",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.building_blocks.siding.title": "Siding",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.building_blocks.stone_patterns": "Every stone is cut into bricks, tiles and a carved creeper face. Stone, granite, diorite, andesite, calcite, tuff, dripstone, deepslate, blackstone, sandstone and red sandstone.\n\nThe stonecutter makes them from the raw stone or from its polished form.",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.building_blocks.stone_patterns.title": "Stone Patterns",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.building_blocks.timber": "The lumber mill cuts every kind of planks into parquet and framed planks.",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.building_blocks.timber.title": "Boards",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.building_blocks.weathering": "Every stone's bricks have a mossy and a cracked form, made the way vanilla stone bricks are. Vines or moss for mossy, a furnace for cracked.",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.building_blocks.weathering.title": "Mossy and Cracked",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.doors": "Doors and Fences",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.doors.chain_link": "Chain link makes a fence you can see through",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.doors.chain_link.title": "Chain Link",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.doors.doors": "Glass, quartz and steel doors, for the places a plank door looks wrong. All three can take a padlock from Assorted Storage like any other door.",
  "manual.assorteddecor.chapter.doors.doors.title": "Doors",
  "manual.assorteddecor.description": "Blocks that take on the look of other blocks, plus furniture, lights, decorations, wall art, roads and more.",
  "manual.assorteddecor.title": "Assorted Decor"
}